sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-anthrobots-09> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-09--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-09--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-anthrobots-09: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.35" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.346"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "needs-new-data" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.76"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Straightness, gyration and a cluster-number criterion are a fully specified reanalysis, and they would separate discrete types from a continuum if the tracks existed. The paper keeps those coordinates on request. Watching representative clips does not rerun the clustering, so the four-type partition is not resolvable from open data." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Recompute straightness and gyration on the 30-second segments from the roughly 200 tracked bots and repeat the unsupervised clustering under the original and under alternative cluster counts. Four groups that align with circular, linear, curvilinear and mixed paths, and that are preferred by a stability criterion, would support discrete types; a continuous cloud or a different preferred count would refute four types." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Trajectory coordinates for the 200 bots are not public.", "Four clusters can be imposed by the choice of k and by the two indices.", "Example videos show one bot of each narrated type, not the sample used for clustering." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-09--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of levin-2024-anthrobots-09 by Grok 4.7: 0.84" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.84"^^xsd:double ;
